From: r56p0 port for the Mali r56p0 x86_64 research kit
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] r56p0: disable the source of the absent arbitration Kconfig

Upstream Arm's 0006-Fix-make-clean-when-no-arbitration-code-present.patch wraps
the arbitration reference in the midgard Kbuild. That patch cannot help here,
for two independent reasons:

  1. The r56p0 Kbuild contains no arbitration reference at all, so there is
     nothing for 0006 to guard.
  2. 0006 never touched the Kconfig, and the Kconfig is what actually breaks.

drivers/gpu/arm/Kconfig unconditionally sources

    source "$(MALI_KCONFIG_EXT_PREFIX)drivers/gpu/arm/arbitration/Kconfig"

but drivers/gpu/arm/ contains only midgard/, there is no arbitration/ directory
anywhere in the release, and CONFIG_MALI_HAS_VIRTUALIZATION is referenced neither
in any Kbuild nor in any Kconfig. MALI_KCONFIG_EXT_PREFIX is never assigned here,
so it expands to nothing. The result is a hard configure failure, before any
patching could be reached:

    drivers/gpu/arm/Kconfig:25: can't open file "drivers/gpu/arm/arbitration/Kconfig"
    make[3]: *** [.../scripts/kconfig/Makefile:85: olddefconfig] Error 1

NOTE ON MECHANISM: the line must be disabled with a "#" comment. Wrapping it in
"#if 0" does NOT work. kconfig includes a sourced file even inside a false
conditional block; this was confirmed empirically against 6.18.55, where the
"#if 0" variant still failed with the error above (reported at the shifted line
number of the still-live source statement).

---
--- a/product/kernel/drivers/gpu/arm/Kconfig
+++ b/product/kernel/drivers/gpu/arm/Kconfig
@@ -22,7 +22,26 @@
 source "$(MALI_KCONFIG_EXT_PREFIX)drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kconfig"
 
 
-source "$(MALI_KCONFIG_EXT_PREFIX)drivers/gpu/arm/arbitration/Kconfig"
+# r56p0 port: this line is DISABLED with a comment, not with "#if 0".
+# kconfig includes a sourced file even inside a false #if block, so "#if 0"
+# does NOT work here; only commenting the line out does. Verified against
+# 6.18.55: "#if 0" still fails olddefconfig with
+#   drivers/gpu/arm/Kconfig:34: can't open file "drivers/gpu/arm/arbitration/Kconfig"
+#
+# Why this is needed: the arbitration reference-code directory is not shipped
+# in the r56p0-18eac0 release. drivers/gpu/arm/ contains only midgard/, there is
+# no arbitration/ anywhere, and CONFIG_MALI_HAS_VIRTUALIZATION is referenced
+# neither in any Kbuild nor in any Kconfig. MALI_KCONFIG_EXT_PREFIX is never
+# assigned in this release, so it expands to nothing.
+#
+# Arm's 0006 does not help: the r56p0 Kbuild has no arbitration reference for it
+# to guard, and 0006 never touched the Kconfig, which is what actually breaks.
+# Guarding is safe because nothing in the release defines or consumes the
+# arbitration symbols, and Arm confirms the arbitration code is optional:
+# "in most cases the Arbitration code is not required, such as in testing
+# systems where only a single Guest OS is using the GPU."
+# (Virtual Platform How-To Guide, Troubleshooting)
+#source "$(MALI_KCONFIG_EXT_PREFIX)drivers/gpu/arm/arbitration/Kconfig"
 
 endmenu
 
